   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "## Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "To prepare the data for financial analysis, returns and log returns are calculated.\n",
    "These transformations help stabilize variance and make the data more suitable for time series modeling.\n",
    "This matters because:\n",
    "-The returns measure percentage change\n",
    "\n",
    "Log returns are used in volatility modeling and financial econometrics"
   ],
   "id": "5d37e3820b33c923"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-05-05T10:55:37.221349600Z",
     "start_time": "2026-05-05T10:55:37.109492100Z"
    }
   },
   "cell_type": "code",
   "source": [
    "# Calculate simple returns\n",
    "data['Returns'] = data['Close'].pct_change()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Calculate log returns\n",
    "data['Log_Returns'] = np.log(data['Close'] / data['Close'].shift(1))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Remove missing values created by shifting\n",
    "data = data.dropna()\n",
    "\n",
    "data.head()"
   ],
