  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "A skewness value close to zero indicates a symmetric distribution.\n",
    "A positive value indicates right skewness, while a negative value indicates left skewness."
   ],
   "id": "bbe50e0b9ffb03a6"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "The computed skewness suggests that the distribution of returns is [positive/negative], indicating asymmetry in the data.",
   "id": "ed4f8b193a7d55b0"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "Skewed data violates the assumption of normality, which can lead to biased statistical results and incorrect financial risk assessments.",
   "id": "8ea7533675b5de3"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {},
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": [
    "To address skewness:\n",
    "- Apply log transformations\n",
    "- Use robust statistical techniques\n",
    "- Consider distributions that account for skewness"
   ],
   "id": "cf4dfd591ea46cdc"
  },
  {
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-05-05T10:55:42.211907900Z",
     "start_time": "2026-05-05T10:55:41.762709500Z"
    }
   },
